00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:37.110
<b>Don't expect a helping hand 
from the Jet-Black Mermaid.</b>

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.030
<b>Okay!</b>

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.800
<b>Teko, I know this is your first sea dive in a dry suit,</b>

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.770
<b>but stick to what you practiced in the pool and you'll be fine.</b>

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:48.590
<b>Right. I'm looking forward to our afternoon boat-diving excursion too. {## unless 'excursion boat' is a thing?}</b>

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.330
<b>Tekochin, you really are extra motivated.</b>

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.040
<b>I simulated this dive in my head a lot in preparation.</b>

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.550
<b>That doesn't mean you can let your guard down.</b>

00:03:58.940 --> 00:03:59.980
<b>Right!</b>

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:14.740
<b>Start off by pressing the exhaust valve on your shoulder to expel the air from your dry suit.</b>

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.070
<b>Okay.</b>

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.450
<b>It's all escaping!</b>

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.160
<b>Do you remember how to use the exhaust valve?</b>

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.150
<b>Um, first you turn it to unlock it and then set the mode to auto. {## 'turn to unlock it' suggests the person turning, 'mode' is not necessary in English}{I don't like all the its}</b>

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.660
<b>That will allow air to escape on its own.</b>

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:34.620
<b>Lock it again once you're underwater, and set it back to auto when you want to ascend.</b>

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.470
<b>Teko, that was perfect!</b>

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.840
<b>You deserve praise for being such a diligent student. {## please no 'studier'}</b>

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.130
<b>I did my best! {## the stock phrase is preferable. alt. 'worked my hardest!', or append 'for this' but the meaning shifts and it's weird}</b>

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.880
<b>All right, is everyone good to go?</b>

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:45.740
<b>Yes!</b>

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.230
<b>Okay! Let's-a... {## left to right: Waluigi, two Marios, Luigi, Wario...?}</b>

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.270
<b>Go!</b>

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:08.530
<b><i>Exhale while descending to compress your lungs.</i></b>

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.990
<b><i>Good, just like I practiced.</i></b>

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:21.050
<b><i>The first thing you do after starting the dive is to create neutral buoyancy.</i></b>

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.200
<b><i>Find the spot where you neither sink nor rise.</i></b>

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.100
<b><i>Adjust it like I would with the air inside my body.</i></b>

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:34.420
<b><i>Did I do it?</i></b>

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.480
<b><i>Yes!</i></b>

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.400
<b><i>Deeper down! {## alt. 'in', both preferable to 'on' (sounds horizontal)}</i></b>

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:51.790
<b><i>The deeper you go, the more the water pressure compresses the air in your suit.</i></b>

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:56.080
<b><i>Don't forget to add just the right amount of air for the depth.</i></b>

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.680
<b><i>Using the inflation valve on my chest to add air...</i></b>

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:02.750
<b><i>There.</i></b>

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:07.680
<b><i>Huh?</i></b>

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:10.610
<b><i>It hasn't stopped tightening. {## 'hasn't' stopped conveys an expectation of a -change in state-, which makes clearer what Teko thought would happen. I initially parsed it as the air was tightening her suit or something weird like that}</i></b>

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:12.460
<b><i>It still hurts.</i></b>

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:15.830
<b><i>Why? There must be a reason.</i></b>

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:20.560
<b><i>When adding air doesn't stop it from tightening, um...</i></b>

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.020
<b><i>Oh, that's right!</i></b>

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.940
<b><i>I forgot to lock the valve on my shoulder!</i></b>

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.540
<b><i>No wonder all the air I was putting in kept escaping.</i></b>

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:32.200
<b><i>Right, Pikari?</i></b>

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:39.790
<b><i>I'm putting in all my effort today!</i></b>

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.930
<b><i>What was that?</i></b>

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:54.930
<b><i>Your regulator is out!</i></b>

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.200
<b><i>Y-You shouldn't do that!</i></b>

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.320
<b><i>It looks like Teko is excited... I think.</i></b>

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.600
<b><i>These are air rings.</i></b>

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.600
<b><i>I've never seen anything like this! {## referent switch, else plural/singular collision with 'air rings'}</i></b>

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:28.210
<b><i>It's like a gleaming dance of light and bubbles!</i></b>

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:37.460
<b><i>Amazing! It's so fun! {sugoooi! tanoshiii!}{## itai~ tanoshii!}</i></b>

00:07:51.930 --> 00:08:01.000
<b><i>Things were a bit iffy earlier, but wouldn't you say I deserve a passing grade, Ooki "Teko" Futaba-san? {she's speaking about herself in the third person}</i></b>

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:10.380
<b><i>Huh? When did everyone else get so much deeper?</i></b>

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.060
<b><i>I have to catch up!</i></b>

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:14.510
<b><i>What?</i></b>

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:18.510
<b><i>Why can't I go down?</i></b>

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:23.340
<b><i>It's because I'm rising rapidly! {## orig. sounds like 'they weren't rising fast'. it's just unworkable because the directions are different, so has to be either generic moving, or rework to something like this}</i></b>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.110
<b><i>No! I'm being pulled!</i></b>

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:28.690
<b><i>Teko!</i></b>

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.570
<b><i>Nothing's coming out! {## I don't want to use 'escaping' more than necessary, it feels a little clunky to me}</i></b>

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:32.440
<b><i>Pikari!</i></b>

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:51.300
<b>Teko.</b>

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.880
<b>Do you understand what happened to you?</b>

00:08:58.690 --> 00:08:59.970
<b>Yes.</b>

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:08.690
<b>Going from a deeper location to a shallower one reduced the water pressure, so the air in my suit expanded. {## is describing specific past, not generic}</b>

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:12.710
<b>As a result, I began to rapidly rise.</b>

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.850
<b>I needed... to let the air escape.</b>

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:20.970
<b>That's right.</b>

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:26.340
<b>I'm sure you also know the dangers of rapid ascents. {## reads as 'you don't, but should'}</b>

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.250
<b>I do.</b>

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:32.040
<b>The nitrogen dissolved in your blood expands, forming air bubbles.</b>

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:36.300
<b>That causes symptoms of numbness and pain.</b>

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.800
<b>And Teko, you also lifted your legs.</b>

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:42.840
<b>The exhaust valve is on your shoulder.</b>

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:47.670
<b>If you allow the air to gather around your legs, it's game over. {## not just -air-, but -all of it-}</b>

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:53.980
<b>I was really looking forward to today.</b>

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:59.530
<b>I wanted to do everything perfectly by myself, like everyone else.</b>

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:04.080
<b>I thought that I had prepared enough to do it.</b>

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.410
<b>Things were going so well as first that I got full of myself. {## orig. 'at first' distributes in undesirable fashion}</b>

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.170
<b>But when they took a turn for the worse, I panicked.</b>

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.670
<b>I completely blanked out.</b>

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.630
<b>It was a total failure.</b>

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.920
<b>I can't believe in myself anymore.</b>

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.720
<b>You know...</b>

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.420
<b>I saw how hard you worked just for today.</b>

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:36.780
<b>You studied so much and practiced so hard.</b>

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.720
<b>I know because I saw it all.</b>

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.240
<b>You were really doing your best!</b>

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:49.940
<b>You seemed to be sparkling when everything was going well, and your smile was so bright.</b>

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:53.970
<b>Being able to dive with you made me happy too, you know.</b>

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.240
<b>Pikari...</b>

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:02.270
<b>So saying you can't believe in yourself anymore just makes me feel bad about how hard you worked.</b>

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:07.910
<b>Sure, your biggest enemy might be your own useless self.</b>

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:08.850
<b>But...</b>

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.440
<b>You're also your own greatest ally when it comes down to it.</b>

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:15.230
<b>Pikari...</b>

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:21.820
<b>So don't say you can't believe in yourself anymore.</b>

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.430
<b>Okay. I'm sorry, Pikari.</b>

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.870
<b>Let's get back in that max motivation mode for dive two.</b>

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.070
<b>Right!</b>

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:46.510
<b>Teko.</b>

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:48.530
<b>You're still feeling down.</b>

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:50.330
<b>Oh, sorry.</b>

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:58.440
<b>I was just thinking about what would've happened if you and Katori-sensei hadn't saved me back then. {## horrible death by bends}</b>

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.190
<b>You overthink things, Tekochin.</b>

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.780
<b>Do I really?</b>

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:07.200
<b>Thinking too hard can sometimes make you so nervous you mess up.</b>

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.250
<b>Yeah, yeah! Don't think, just do! {## parallelism precedes yattemiyou}</b>

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.490
<b>Though Bakari would do well to think more.  {## orig. 'Not thinking is fine, look at Pikari' as opposed to well, this}</b>

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.170
<b>Yeah.</b>

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:20.060
<b>I should just think about what I want to do instead of worrying. {## one way ticket to bendstown}</b>

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:21.010
<b>That's the way!</b>

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:25.260
<b>I want to dive as much as I can with all of you!</b>

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.740
<b>I want to be able to confidently say that I'm Pikari's buddy!</b>

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.040
<b>Yay!</b>

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.510
<b>Grandma!</b>

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.070
<b>I brought this over... {## what a CUTE}</b>

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.710
<b>Kodama-chan!</b>

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:41.740
<b>What's the occasion? You almost never come here!</b>

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.050
<b>Mom asked me to deliver this.</b>

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.740
<b>Ah, it's Gramps' bath towel.</b>

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:49.990
<b>Some things never change.</b>

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.400
<b>It's huge!</b>

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.870
<b>You said it was a bath towel, didn't you?</b>

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.610
<b>Are you sure that's not a bed sheet?</b>

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:59.340
<b>It's Gramps' personal bath towel.</b>

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:01.470
<b>Thanks, Kodama.</b>

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:02.660
<b>Sure.</b>

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:04.800
<b>Excuse me.</b>

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.210
<b>Do you happen to be Pikari's...</b>

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:09.630
<b>Yes, my sister Kodama-chan!</b>

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:10.630
<b>I knew it!</b>

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:14.410
<b>Now that you mention it, I can kind of see the resemblance. {for the record, this was on purpose}</b>

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:15.600
<b>Right?</b>

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:17.700
<b>You're sweaty!</b>

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:23.320
<b>Dry suits make you sweat a lot, 
so be careful not to catch a cold.</b>

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:29.220
<b>Could it be that you've been reading up on diving?</b>

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:32.490
<b>Could it be that you want to dive again?</b>

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.290
<b>Why would I?</b>

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:36.660
<b>It's common sense that dry suits make you sweat. {## 'common sense' being an application of reason, and leading to a much more unwieldy 'Understanding that dry suits must make you sweat is only common sense' or something}{I can fix this using some common sense}</b>

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:37.920
<b>Ah, okay.</b>

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.870
<b>She's got a good head on her shoulders.</b>

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:42.460
<b>Kodama-chan, you have experience diving too?</b>

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.700
<b>We used to go all the time back in elementary school.</b>

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.930
<b>In fact, I still have my Junior Diver C-card. {## 'technically' sounds like it's kind of sketchy or something, or she's lacking some other qualification, but i think she just doesn't use it. for the fourth time: ichiou, the worst}</b>

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.810
<b>That makes you like my role model!</b>

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:57.780
<b>It's just amazing that you've been part of that blue world since you were in elementary!</b>

00:13:57.780 --> 00:13:59.540
<b>Is it all thanks to your sister?</b>

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:01.820
<b>Well, I guess you could say that.</b>

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:06.650
<b>I used to get dragged around everywhere by my airheaded sister.</b>

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:11.550
<b>Always following one step behind her aggressive way of playing was more than just annoying— {## 'being' more like she wants to be lockstepped to the dumb aguresshibuness}</b>

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.370
<b>sometimes it even got us into deep trouble. {## 'almost'? not 'even'?}</b>

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.640
<b>I'm glad to say I've found my independence since then.</b>

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.130
<b>We haven't gone diving together in years.</b>

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.230
<b>Sounds like you had it rough.</b>

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.850
<b>It's the same for younger siblings everywhere.</b>

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.360
<b>You must be Teko-san, right?</b>

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:30.260
<b>Oh, yes.</b>

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:34.420
<b>Please continue looking after my sister!</b>

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.060
<b>I will be under her care as well!</b>

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.530
<b>Talk about a respectable little sister.</b>

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.490
<b>They went back-first...</b>

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.940
<b>That's called a back roll entry.</b>

00:14:55.940 --> 00:15:01.860
<b>You can also stand on the edge of the boat and throw yourself off with one huge step.</b>

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.630
<b>That's called the giant stride.</b>

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:05.550
<b>Think you can do it?</b>

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:08.760
<b>Yeah!</b>

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:12.470
<b>Good answer, Teko! Very good!</b>

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.300
<b>Sea surface, clear! {## what does this mean?}{nobody to jump on top of}</b>

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:16.560
<b>S-Sea surface, clear!</b>

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:22.040
<b>Now then, hold your mask and regulator firmly so they don't get dislodged by the force of entry.</b>

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:22.930
<b>Okay!</b>

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.820
<b>We can fly! {## so why doesn't this obliterate your crotch? do your legs break the surface tension?}{1, their legs aren't spread, 2, they're wearing drysuits}</b>

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.980
<b><i>Thank goodness. This is going much more smoothly than earlier.</i></b>

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:15.890
<b><i>Open water divers can't descent past a depth of eighteen meters. {## i know it's 'made', and i know i'm the one who reasons with 'shika' and 'dake', but orig. was weird in English for some reason}</i></b>

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.280
We're stuck behind

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:22.060
<b><i>I want to get my Advanced qualification soon! {## see earlier instance}</i></b>

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:25.750
<b><i>The Jet-Black Mermaid?!</i></b>

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.620
<b><i>Just a sea turtle.</i></b>

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:38.220
<b><i>Pikari! It's a sea turtle! My first one ever!</i></b>

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.500
<b><i>Well, I'm not surprised.</i></b>

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.700
<b><i>There's no way the Jet-Black Mermaid actually—</i></b>

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:59.330
<b><i>What... was that?</i></b>

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.040
<b><i>It was swimming too fast to see.</i></b>

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.290
<b><i>Mato-chan-sensei!</i></b>

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:04.540
<b><i>Look out!</i></b>

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.120
<b><i>A completely black wetsuit.</i></b>

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.760
<b><i>Coming to rescue you when you run into trouble. {## nominal fragmentary, parallel / he -caused- the trouble, though}</i></b>

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.590
<b><i>Is this the Jet-Black—</i></b>

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:20.510
<b><i>Mer...maid?</i></b>

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:23.770
<b><i>He's huge!</i></b>

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:49.200
<b><i>There's no telling whether he's the real deal or not,</i></b>

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.920
<b><i>but it's all or nothing!</i></b>

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.040
<b><i>He says to hold on tight. {## alt. just 'grip tightly', introduction of 'our hands' conflicts with subject a bit and it gets weird}</i></b>

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:32.750
<b><i>We aren't even swimming, yet he's pulling us at this speed.</i></b>

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:56.490
<b><i>Th-This truly is...</i></b>

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:58.760
<b><i>The Dragon Palace!</i></b>

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:14.380
<b><i>It's beautiful.</i></b>

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.730
<b><i>We went so quickly...</i></b>

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:37.650
<b><i>that I don't even have a clue where that was. {## 'we went' half applies to their current position. initially I parsed this as them being not where they originally were}</i></b>

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:42.080
<b><i>He really must be the legendary mermaid.</i></b>

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:46.580
<b><i>I met him... I actually met him!</i></b>

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.080
<b>For real?!</b>

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:52.670
<b>And then we were back to where we started in a flash.</b>

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:58.960
<b>The legendary Jet-Black Mermaid... That's unbelievable.</b>

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.300
<b>I know, but he's real!</b>

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.260
<b>I wanted to see him too!</b>

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:06.360
<b><i>Floating and falling, floating and falling.</i></b>

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:09.480
<b><i>I haven't felt this way in a long time.</i></b>

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:12.190
<b><i>I wonder why...</i></b>

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.980
<b><i>It doesn't feel like this is the first time we've met.</i></b>

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:20.850
<b>Huh? {## ?!}</b>

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:22.400
<b>Katori-sensei!</b>

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.820
<b>Do you think we'll meet him again? {## 'meet again' being Katori and Teko}</b>

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:26.320
<b>I'm sure of it.</b>

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:28.950
<b>Though I'm sick and tired of emergencies.</b>

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:33.070
<b>Hey, you think that must have been the Dragon Palace too, right? {## alt. 'think that was the', careful about the tenses here}</b>

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:35.350
<b>Yep, it couldn't have been anywhere else.</b>

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:37.460
<b>Right? It was just so beautiful.</b>

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:42.050
<b>Tekochin, you can't stop smiling? {## I don't like the way this is a question but I really can't do anything about it?}</b>

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:47.430
<b>No way! I never could've even dreamed that I'd see a mermaid and the Dragon Palace! {## that was no mermaid, Tek}</b>

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:51.270
<b>Everything I planned in advance went badly,</b>

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:54.390
<b>but everything that was unexpected made today unforgettable!</b>

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:56.400
<b>What a surprise!</b>

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.980
<b>I think it must've been a reward for all your hard work.</b>

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:03.220
<b>Not a bad line coming from you, Makoto.</b>

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.700
<b>Give me a break.</b>

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:08.660
<b>But if he's right,</b>

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:13.660
<b>do you think the part of me that worked hard ended up becoming my ally?</b>

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:15.870
<b>Yeah, definitely!</b>

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:21.100
<b>Oh? This morning's max-motivation-mode Tekochin is finally back! {## precedes noun (think of 'Type-A' or something)}</b>

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:21.840
<b>Yes!</b>

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:23.810
<b>I'm super max motivated!</b>

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:26.920
<b>I want to visit the Dragon Palace again no matter what!</b>

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:29.490
<b>Also, I want to see the mermaid again!</b>

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:34.890
<b>I was totally blindsided.</b>

00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:38.750
<b>Gramps, people are calling you the Jet-Black Mermaid. {## these are actually quite necessary, since without implies that there's a different Jet-Black Mermaid they're mistaking him for (italics 'you', for example)}</b>

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:39.900
<b>Ew, gross!</b>

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:42.910
<b>He doesn't really fit the image.</b>

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:46.580
<b>There's even legends about him. {## should be 'are' but this is 'if it was' territory}</b>

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.330
<b>And not just that...</b>

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:58.500
<b>Hello, hello, hello!</b>

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:58.500
<b>Hello, hello, hello!</b>

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:10.620
<b>Close your eyes and imagine what you'll be like when you're older</b>

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:10.620
<b>souzou shitemirunda itsuka toshi wo totta toki</b>

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:18.110
<b>What things will you look back on fondly?</b>

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:18.110
<b>donna koto wo natsukashiku omou no darou</b>

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:25.460
<b>Maybe your mother's favorite phrase</b>

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:25.460
<b>haha no kuchiguse to ka</b>

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:35.370
<b>Maybe the first time you ever flipped over a gym bar</b>

